            <div xml:id="d966">

                <pb facs="0742" n="626" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg626"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13858.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Brazilian Minister to
                        Mexico to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brazilian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-22T11:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 22, 1914, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>218. General Blanco today assumed full command of the situation in the Federal
                    District, appointing provisionally governor, police inspector and minor
                    officials. I was reliably informed that this took place after serious
                    disagreement between him and Obregón who as his senior officer commanded him to
                    abandon the city, which he strongly refused to do.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cardoso de Oliveira</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
